---
# clang-tidy configuration for this project's own code, under src/.
#
# It lives at the repository root so every first-party tree resolves to it by
# clang-tidy's parent-directory search, and so tools invoked from the root
# (run-clang-tidy, IDEs) find a config at all instead of failing with "No checks
# enabled". Vendored code under _deps/ is kept out of linting by CMake, which
# clears CMAKE_CXX_CLANG_TIDY across the dependency fetch -- see the top-level
# CMakeLists.txt. This is the only .clang-tidy in the tree, deliberately: one
# style, one config, no module-local overrides to diverge from it.
#
# Every check below is a hard error, so a suppression is a real decision. A bare
# `-some-check` with no rationale is indistinguishable from an accident, and every
# entry in the list that follows carries the number of sites it actually silences
# **in this project**, measured by running that check alone over every first-party
# translation unit. If a number here is zero, delete the suppression instead of
# keeping it.
#
# That measurement is worth repeating after a toolchain bump, and worth repeating
# for a reason: this file arrived from another project, and for a long time it
# justified its suppressions with that project's code -- a terminal emulator's
# grid buffers, its VT dispatch switch, its pty read under a mutex, and site
# counts in the thousands taken from a tree an order of magnitude larger. None of
# it was true here. Re-measuring dropped 38 suppressions that silenced nothing at
# all, and turned two more into four-line fixes.
#
# Suppressions, most-silenced first, with what each one actually covers here:
#
#   382  cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-avoid-unchecked-container-access
#    85  cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-constant-array-index
#         The driver indexes fixed-size std::arrays by enumerator -- indexOf(knob),
#         indexOf(mix) -- and reads reports at protocol constants. The index is a
#         table position or a wire offset, both checked by static_assert or by the
#         decoder's length guard, so a bounds-checked accessor moves the check to
#         run time without adding one.
#     2  cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-pointer-arithmetic -- argv, twice.
#
#   356  modernize-use-trailing-return-type -- house style is leading.
#   354  misc-include-cleaner -- a real backlog, not a policy. Nothing pursues it
#         yet; turning it on today would be 354 errors in one commit.
#   278  readability-magic-numbers
#   278  cppcoreguidelines-avoid-magic-numbers  (the same check, other name)
#         Protocol offsets and interface geometry. The protocol's numbers are named
#         in Protocol.hpp and the check cannot see that a literal at a call site is
#         one of them.
#   227  readability-braces-around-statements
#     2  readability-inconsistent-ifelse-braces  (the same area)
#         Brace style is settled by .clang-format.
#    37  readability-identifier-length -- `i`, `x`, `y` are fine.
#    24  portability-avoid-pragma-once -- `#pragma once` is the house include guard.
#    15  misc-non-private-member-variables-in-classes
#     0  cppcoreguidelines-non-private-member-variables-in-classes (same check, and
#         off so that enabling one name does not silently re-enable the other)
#         Test fixtures whose members the test bodies drive directly, and
#         UsbmonCapture::Record, which is a wire record rather than a class.
#    10  readability-implicit-bool-conversion -- all in HidApiTransport.cpp, where
#         hidapi is a C API returning pointers and `if (device)` is its idiom.
#     8  modernize-use-scoped-lock -- eight std::lock_guards over one mutex each.
#         scoped_lock exists for the multi-mutex case, which does not occur here.
#     8  bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters -- (mix, knob) and (x, y) pairs. The
#         check flags the shape rather than a defect.
#     4  bugprone-exception-escape -- three main()s and ~Device.
#     4  cppcoreguidelines-owning-memory -- QCoreApplication::postEvent takes
#         ownership of the QMouseEvent it is given; that is Qt's contract.
#     2  readability-convert-member-functions-to-static -- trackNames() and
#         parameters() are Q_PROPERTY getters. Making them static changes what QML
#         binds to.
#     1  bugprone-branch-clone -- two pcap magics that mean the same endianness.
#         Merging them would hide that there are two.
#     1  bugprone-unchecked-optional-access -- ILogger_test.cpp guards with
#         REQUIRE(...has_value()), which the check cannot see through.
#     1  cppcoreguidelines-avoid-non-const-global-variables -- a Qt message handler
#         is a plain function pointer with nowhere to hang state.
#     1  cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-reinterpret-cast -- QByteArray's char to the
#         driver's std::uint8_t, at the one place Qt meets the wire.
#     1  misc-multiple-inheritance -- `struct Overloaded: Ts...`, the visitor idiom.
#     0  bugprone-chained-comparison -- the one entry kept without a number.
#         CHECK(a == b) expands to `Catch::Decomposer() <= a == b`, a chained
#         comparison by construction, so it fires on ordinary assertions depending
#         on how Catch2 is included. A local sweep can measure zero and CI still
#         fail, which is exactly what happened while measuring this list.

Checks: >-
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  -bugprone-branch-clone,
  -bugprone-chained-comparison,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -bugprone-exception-escape,
  -bugprone-unchecked-optional-access,
  clang-analyzer-core.*,
  clang-analyzer-cplusplus.*,
  clang-analyzer-deadcode.*,
  clang-analyzer-nullability.*,
  clang-analyzer-optin.cplusplus.*,
  clang-analyzer-optin.performance.*,
  clang-analyzer-optin.portability.*,
  clang-analyzer-security.*,
  clang-analyzer-unix.*,
  clang-diagnostic-*,
  concurrency-*,
  cppcoreguidelines-*,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-magic-numbers,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-non-const-global-variables,
  -cppcoreguidelines-non-private-member-variables-in-classes,
  -cppcoreguidelines-owning-memory,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-avoid-unchecked-container-access,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-constant-array-index,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-pointer-arithmetic,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-reinterpret-cast,
  # Catches includes that are unsorted WITHIN a block. It does not read
  # .clang-format's IncludeCategories and cannot see a block in the wrong place,
  # so it is not what keeps this project's own headers first -- measured, after
  # assuming otherwise. scripts/check-include-order.py is what does that, and it
  # runs as a test.
  llvm-include-order,
  misc-*,
  -misc-include-cleaner,
  -misc-multiple-inheritance,
  -misc-non-private-member-variables-in-classes,
  modernize-*,
  -modernize-use-scoped-lock,
  -modernize-use-trailing-return-type,
  performance-*,
  portability-*,
  -portability-avoid-pragma-once,
  readability-*,
  -readability-braces-around-statements,
  -readability-convert-member-functions-to-static,
  -readability-identifier-length,
  -readability-implicit-bool-conversion,
  -readability-inconsistent-ifelse-braces,
  -readability-magic-numbers,

# Every enabled check is a hard error. Fix the cause rather than adding a NOLINT;
# if a check is wrong often enough to need one, it belongs in the list above with
# its count.
WarningsAsErrors: '*'

UseColor: true
# Every first-party header, not only the two module directories. src/tools/ and
# src/tests/ were outside this and so went unlinted entirely -- which is how
# UsbmonCapture.hpp and ReportBuilder.hpp came to be the only headers nothing
# checked.
HeaderFilterRegex: 'src/(ax310|app|tools|tests)/'
# Qt's AUTOMOC/AUTOUIC output lands under out/<preset>/src/<module>/..._autogen/,
# whose path matches HeaderFilterRegex; it is generated code and not ours to lint.
ExcludeHeaderFilterRegex: '.*_autogen/.*|.*\.moc$'
FormatStyle: none

CheckOptions:
  cppcoreguidelines-explicit-virtual-functions.IgnoreDestructors: '1'
  modernize-loop-convert.MaxCopySize: '16'
  modernize-loop-convert.MinConfidence: reasonable
  modernize-loop-convert.NamingStyle: CamelCase
  modernize-pass-by-value.IncludeStyle: llvm
  modernize-replace-auto-ptr.IncludeStyle: llvm
  modernize-use-default-member-init.UseAssignment: '1'
  modernize-use-nullptr.NullMacros: 'NULL'
  # Pointer analysis proposes a const *pointee* where only the pointer itself could be
  # const, which is a different guarantee and breaks callers that write through it.
  misc-const-correctness.AnalyzePointers: 'false'
  readability-function-cognitive-complexity.Threshold: '50'
  readability-function-cognitive-complexity.IgnoreMacros: 'true'

  # Identifier naming. Types are CamelCase, everything else camelBack, with a
  # leading underscore on non-public data members. This block is what makes that
  # rule enforceable rather than aspirational, so a category missing from it is a
  # category nothing checks: functions, methods and type aliases went unchecked
  # tree-wide until they were added here, and snake_case survived a whole-tree
  # rename sweep with a clean build to prove it.
  #
  # The names the standard library binds to *by spelling* -- member typedefs
  # (value_type, iterator, difference_type), container methods (begin,
  # push_back), std::formatter/std::hash specializations -- cannot follow this
  # rule and carry a NOLINT(readability-identifier-naming) with their reason at
  # the declaration.
  readability-identifier-naming.ClassCase: CamelCase
  readability-identifier-naming.ClassConstantCase: CamelCase
  readability-identifier-naming.ClassMemberCase: CamelCase
  readability-identifier-naming.ClassMethodCase: camelBack
  readability-identifier-naming.ConstantCase: camelBack
  readability-identifier-naming.ConstantMemberCase: camelBack
  readability-identifier-naming.ConstantMemberPrefix: '_'
  readability-identifier-naming.ConstexprVariableCase: CamelCase
  readability-identifier-naming.EnumCase: CamelCase
  readability-identifier-naming.EnumConstantCase: CamelCase
  readability-identifier-naming.FunctionCase: camelBack
  readability-identifier-naming.MethodCase: camelBack
  readability-identifier-naming.ParameterCase: camelBack
  readability-identifier-naming.PrivateMemberCase: camelBack
  readability-identifier-naming.PrivateMemberPrefix: '_'
  readability-identifier-naming.ProtectedMemberCase: camelBack
  readability-identifier-naming.ProtectedMemberPrefix: '_'
  readability-identifier-naming.PublicMemberCase: camelBack
  readability-identifier-naming.ScopedEnumConstantCase: CamelCase
  readability-identifier-naming.StructCase: CamelCase
  readability-identifier-naming.TypeAliasCase: CamelCase
  readability-identifier-naming.TypedefCase: CamelCase
  readability-identifier-naming.TypeTemplateParameterCase: CamelCase
  readability-identifier-naming.UnionCase: CamelCase
  readability-identifier-naming.VariableCase: camelBack
  readability-identifier-naming.GlobalVariableCase: camelBack
  # No Hungarian notation: no g/s_/k prefixes. Globals are plain camelBack.
